Package: irtalign
Type: Package
Title: Alignment Optimization for Multiple-Group Item Response Models
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Yonggi", "Kim", email = "yonggi1124@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Estimates group-specific latent means and variances across many
    groups without exact measurement invariance, using the alignment
    optimization method of Asparouhov and Muthen (2014)
    <doi:10.1080/10705511.2014.919210> and its item response theory
    application (Muthen and Asparouhov, 2014) <doi:10.3389/fpsyg.2014.00978>.
    Dichotomous (2PL, 3PL) and polytomous (graded response and generalized
    partial credit) items can be mixed in one analysis. Provides standard
    errors by implicit differentiation, parameter-by-group noninvariance
    detection, invariance R-squared, simplicity function contributions and
    factor mean comparisons. Group-specific models are estimated with 'mirt'
    (Chalmers, 2012) <doi:10.18637/jss.v048.i06>.
